  <para unique="1046088">
   <string>The source operand is a ZMM/YMM/XMM register, a 512/256/128-bit memory location, or a 512/256/128-bit vector broadcasted from a 64-bit memory location.</string></para>
  <para unique="1046089">
   <string>EVEX.vvvv is reserved and must be 1111b otherwise instructions will #UD.</string></para>
  </longdesc>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting><string>VFPCLASSPD __mmask8 _mm512_fpclass_pd_mask( __m512d a, int c);</string><string>
</string><string>VFPCLASSPD __mmask8 _mm512_mask_fpclass_pd_mask( __mmask8 m, __m512d a, int c)</string><string>
</string><string>VFPCLASSPD __mmask8 _mm256_fpclass_pd_mask( __m256d a, int c)</string><string>
</string><string>VFPCLASSPD __mmask8 _mm256_mask_fpclass_pd_mask( __mmask8 m, __m256d a, int c)</string><string>
</string><string>VFPCLASSPD __mmask8 _mm_fpclass_pd_mask( __m128d a, int c)</string><string>
</string><string>VFPCLASSPD __mmask8 _mm_mask_fpclass_pd_mask( __mmask8 m, __m128d a, int c)</string><string>
</string></programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1046145">
   <string>None.</string></para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Other Exceptions">
  <para unique="1046150">
   <string>See </string><link linkend="79250: 06_Table: Table 2-49. Type E4 Class Exception Conditions"><string>Table&#160;2&#8209;51, &#8220;Type E4 Class Exception Conditions.&#8221;</string></link></para>
  <para unique="1046151">
   <string>Additionally:</string></para>
  <variablelist>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term><string>#UD</string></term>
    <listitem><string>If EVEX.vvvv != 1111B.</string></listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   </variablelist>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
